<!--
PURPOSE
  Adhesion (kPa) is a ratio: peak force / plaque area. Script 3 models adhesion. This
  script fits the same per-animal ANCOVA (01_code/_ancova.R) to its two parts separately,
  plus extension at break, so that an arm difference in adhesion can be traced to force,
  to plaque area, or both. Two arms with the same difference in the ratio can differ in how
  its parts moved.

      log(day-3 level) ~ arm + log(baseline level)     force, area (per-animal geometric means)
      day-3 extension  ~ arm + baseline extension      extension (per-animal means, mm)

  Arms were assigned at random. Each stressor arm is compared with the day-3 treatment
  control, unadjusted and Dunnett-adjusted over the three comparisons.

INPUT
  03_analyses/thread-summary.xlsx, sheet "data" - the same curated table script 3 reads.
  03_analyses/03_analyze-thread-strength/STATS_ancova_vs_control.csv - script 3's adhesion
  result, read only to draw adhesion beside its parts in FIG_ancova_vs_control.png.

OUTPUT  03_analyses/04_decompose-adhesion/
  STATS_ancova_tests.csv               F for arm and for baseline, per response
  STATS_ancova_coefficients.csv        lm coefficients with 95% CI
  STATS_ancova_adjusted_means.csv      arm means at the mean baseline
  STATS_ancova_vs_control.csv          each arm vs control: ratio or difference, 95% CI, p
                                       unadjusted and Dunnett-adjusted
  DATA_ancova_animals.csv              the per-animal rows each model was fitted to
  DIAG_ancova_residuals.png            Q-Q and residuals vs fitted, per response
  FIG_ancova_vs_control.png            each arm vs control, adhesion and its parts
  mussel_response_classification.csv  per-animal description, handed to gene-mechanics
  FIG_animal_response_force_vs_area.png
  STATS_failure_mode.csv               failure-mode counts by thread treatment + chi-square
                                       + Fisher's exact (Monte Carlo) p for the day-3 arms
  FIG_failure_mode_by_arm.png          failure-mode composition by thread treatment
-->

